  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3203.44 Renewable energy projects",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3203.44 “Renewable energy projects” means power generation during the current control period from technologies that produce electricity from small-scale hydro energy, geothermal energy, fuel cells, wind energy, solar thermal energy, photovoltaics, methane waste, or biomass-to-energy plants. The term does not include power generation from combustion or pyrolysis of municipal solid waste, demolition waste, or construction waste.\n\nSource. #11001, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14632, eff 6-25-26, EXPIRES: 6-25-36 (formerly Env-A 3203.48)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3200.html"
